# ================================
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.pyo

# ================================
# Django
# ================================
# NOTE: db.sqlite3 is deliberately NOT ignored, and that is not an oversight.
# Assignment 4 requires the SQLite database to be committed and pushed with the code, so the
# grader (and PythonAnywhere) gets the demo data by cloning the repo instead of having to run
# `migrate` + `seed_demo` first. Please do not "fix" this by adding db.sqlite3 back: the
# assignment is checked against the data in it.
#
# ASSIGNMENT 5 CHANGED WHAT IS IN THE FILE, so the sentence that used to sit here -- "it holds
# nothing secret" -- is no longer true and has been removed rather than left to be believed.
# The database now has an auth_user table (password hashes, real email addresses) and a
# django_session table. The session table is the sharp one: a Django session_key IS the value
# of the sessionid cookie, so a committed session row is a password-free login to the deployed
# site for anybody who can read this repository, and it stays valid for two weeks. Every
# `runserver` you log into while testing writes one.
#
# BEFORE YOU COMMIT THIS FILE, RUN:
#
#     python manage.py scrub_db            # reports what must not be committed
#     python manage.py scrub_db --apply    # empties django_session
#
# It also reports the accounts in the file and any allauth SocialApp rows (which would hold a
# Google client SECRET in plain text -- this project keeps Google credentials in .env instead,
# see docs/a5/google-oauth-setup.md). `manage.py clearsessions` is NOT a substitute: it deletes
# only sessions that have already expired, which is precisely the set that cannot be replayed.
#
# (The usual rule -- a database is data, not code, and belongs outside version control -- is
# the right end state here, with `seed_demo` shipping the demo data instead of this file.)

# Generated by `collectstatic`: a copy of static/ plus hashed filenames. Build output, so it is
# rebuilt on the server and never committed.
staticfiles/
media/
*.log

